Rationale: The claim has three material parts: (1) the Minardi M189 was replaced by a newer model, (2) Pirelli made the tires and headlights for the newer version, and (3) Frank Gardner was a racing driver in the series. The first part is partially supported by the evidence that the M189 was part of the 1989 Formula One World Championship, but no evidence identifies the newer model that replaced it. The second part is entirely unsupported, as no evidence confirms Pirelli's involvement with the newer version. The third part is also unsupported, as no evidence identifies Frank Gardner as a racing driver in the series. Further investigation is required to confirm or refute these missing details.
